-- title:
--   Variable change induces an isomorphism of projective Weierstrass models
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring, let $W$ be a projective Weierstrass cubic over $T$, and let $C=(u,r,s,t)$ be a Weierstrass variable change over $T$. For a projective cubic $V$ write $\mathrm{ProjModelRingCR}(V)$ for the quotient of $T[X_0,X_1,X_2]$ by the ideal generated by the Weierstrass polynomial of $V$, graded by `projModelGradingCR V`, the family of images of the homogeneous submodules of $T[X_0,X_1,X_2]$ under the quotient map, and let `projModelStrCR V` be the structure morphism $\operatorname{Proj}(\mathrm{projModelGradingCR}\,V)\to\operatorname{Spec} T$ obtained from `Proj.toSpecZero` followed by the `Spec`-map of $T \to (\mathrm{projModelGradingCR}\,V)_0$. The assertion is that there exist a graded ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `projModelGradingCR W` to `projModelGradingCR (C • W)` and a proof $h_\varphi$ that the irrelevant ideal of the target grading is contained in the $\varphi$-image of the irrelevant ideal of the source grading, such that: (i) $\varphi$ fixes the classes of constants, sends the class of $X_0$ to that of $u^2X_0+rX_2$, the class of $X_1$ to that of $u^3X_1+u^2sX_0+tX_2$, and the class of $X_2$ to that of $X_2$; (ii) the induced morphism $\operatorname{Proj}(\varphi,h_\varphi)\colon \operatorname{Proj}(\mathrm{projModelGradingCR}(C\bullet W))\to\operatorname{Proj}(\mathrm{projModelGradingCR}\,W)$ is an isomorphism; and (iii) this morphism followed by `projModelStrCR W` equals `projModelStrCR (C • W)`, so the isomorphism is one of $T$-schemes.
--
--   This is the change-of-coordinates invariance of the projective model of a Weierstrass cubic, in the form of an explicit graded substitution inducing an isomorphism of $\operatorname{Proj}$-schemes over the base. It is the variable-change half of the transport of Drinfeld level data along isomorphisms of Weierstrass curves, and is invoked throughout the construction of charts and level structures on modular curves in this development.
